package ai.nisu.assistant

/**
 * v3.84: VIDEO EDITING KNOWLEDGE ONLY. Everything that made her work in a video editor (the slow, careful tapping mode, the extra pauses, the editing
 * reminders in every screen result, the edit_guide tool and its automatic Screen Share) is removed. What stays is what she KNOWS about editing in
 * CapCut / InShot, so she can explain it to him in words. She does not start editing on the screen by herself.
 * The names are those of the English CapCut app; versions and languages differ.
 */
object EditGuide {
    const val KNOWLEDGE = """

VIDEO EDITING KNOWLEDGE (CapCut / InShot; knowledge only: you EXPLAIN how to do an edit, step by step, in his language and in a few clear lines; you do not start editing on his screen by yourself). Names are from the English CapCut app and can differ in his version, so say so when unsure. [new project] Open CapCut. On the home screen tap the big 'New project' (+). Tab Videos (or Photos): tap the video (a number appears on it). Tap 'Add' at the bottom right. The editor opens with the timeline. [trim split delete] Tap the clip on the timeline (white border). Swipe the timeline sideways so the white playhead is exactly where the cut goes. Bottom toolbar 'Edit' > 'Split'. To delete a part: tap that part, 'Edit' > 'Delete' (bin). To trim an end: select the clip and drag the white handle at its left or right end. [speed] Select the clip. Toolbar 'Edit' (or directly 'Speed') > 'Speed' > 'Normal'. Drag the slider (1x is normal, higher = faster). Check mark to apply. [volume music] Clip volume: select the clip > 'Volume' > slider > check. Add music: tap empty space on the timeline so nothing is selected > 'Audio' > 'Sounds' (or 'Device' for his own files) > tap the song > the + button. Drag the music bar to where it should start. [text captions] Text: toolbar 'Text' > 'Add text' > type > check mark; drag the text in the preview to place it; drag its bar on the timeline for the length. Auto captions: 'Captions' > 'Auto captions' > choose the language > 'Start matching' and wait until it finishes. [filters effects] Filters: toolbar 'Filters' > pick one > slider for strength > check. Effects: 'Effects' > 'Video effects' > pick > check (it starts at the playhead). Adjust brightness / contrast: 'Adjust'. [transition] Tap the small white square between two clips on the timeline > pick a transition > set the length > check. [ratio canvas] With nothing selected: toolbar 'Ratio' (or 'Canvas') > 9:16 for stories / reels, 16:9 wide, 1:1 square. [export] Tap 'Export' (top right, arrow). Check the settings chip at the top (for example 1080p / 30fps), then 'Export' again. WAIT until the progress finishes (do not leave the screen). Then it shows 'Done'; the video is saved in the gallery. Share only if he asks."""
}
